# Temporal reads of BOXED values in an UNOBSERVED program — the corner round 36
# claimed closed and did not.
#
# THE POINT OF THIS FIXTURE is that an intersection has as many corners as
# axes. Round 36's fixture filled {temporal} x {boxed} x {OBSERVED} and its
# commit said "the intersection was empty, t113 fills it" — but the unobserved
# corner stayed empty, and a four-line program showed it:
#
#   s is "alpha" / s is "beta" / print of (prev of s)
#   VM  alpha        AOT  null        both build, both rc 0
#
# The boxed assign path had NEVER traced: only the numeric path carried
# aot_trace_assign. Three arms needed the call — the terminal boxed store, the
# lowered-local store, and the numeric-RHS-to-demoted-name store — each staged
# through a temp so the RHS is emitted once. A claim that an intersection is
# closed must name every axis it was closed along.

s is "alpha"
s is "beta"
print of (prev of s)

# the lowered-local arm, inside a function
define f(k) as:
    local t is "aa"
    t is "bb"
    print of (prev of t)
    return 0

print of (f of 1)

# a container: the tape's heap borrow must survive the reassignment that frees
# the old value (history increfs the borrowed slot)
d is {"k": 1}
d is {"k": 2}
print of ((prev of d)["k"])

# and the demoted-numeric arm: a name that later holds a string is off the
# numeric class, so its numeric assigns take the env_write_num path
m is 5
m is 6
print of (prev of m)
m is "end"
print of (prev of m)

# CROSS-FUNCTION: the VM's tape is process-global and NAME-KEYED, so an
# assignment inside an interrogate-free function lands in the same history a
# module-level `prev of` reads. g_traced was derived per function, making the
# write-set scope-local:
#
#   define g(k) as: local s is "one" / s is "two" ... / g of 1 / s is "three"
#   print of (prev of s):   VM  two        AOT  null      both rc 0
#
# Tracing is now program-wide: any interrogate anywhere makes every function
# trace. (A function local SHADOWING a module name refuses loudly under the
# pre-existing temporal-shadow guard -- correct, since the name-keyed tape
# genuinely merges those histories.)
w is "zero"

define gg(k) as:
    # an OUTWARD write to the module-bound w -- no local declaration, so the
    # store crosses the frame and must land on the tape (a local SHADOWING a
    # module name refuses loudly instead, under the temporal-shadow guard)
    w is "two"
    return 0

print of (gg of 1)
w is "three"
print of (prev of w)
print of "done"
